CORE
main.c
--mmio
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^Instrumenting memory-mapped I/O$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
OUTPUT address_of\("volatile-write"
--
^Unknown option
--
--mmio is the entry point for the memory-mapped I/O memory model. It must be a
registered option (not "Unknown option") and currently applies the device
environment model to volatile accesses: the read-back of reg is
non-deterministic (so the assertion fails) and the write to reg is preserved as
an observable side effect (an OUTPUT).
